# Chapter 6, third part: the Printer.  Included by the chapter file.  Its
# command line and the print and preview modes of the Editor are not a
# supported way to start Strata: they are in the last part of the chapter,
# which the release edition leaves out.

.h2 The Printer [print-strprint]
.ix Printer, the typesetter
.ix Typesetter
.ix PDF from a document
.ix TeX file
.ix LaTeX source
The Printer is the part of Strata that turns a document into a typeset file.
The Editor uses it for every Draft, Final and Preview, with no screen of its
own.

.h3 What the Printer makes
.table 20 40
Result | What it is
A PDF file | The pages of Draft and of Final.
The pages of Preview | What the Viewer shows.
The LaTeX source | The file that {k:F12}, File, Export, Export a LaTeX File
 | saves ({n:print-export-latex}).  You can edit it and run LaTeX yourself.
.end
When the Printer makes a file, characters that no font has are printed as
[U+XXXX], and a piece that LaTeX does not accept (an equation, a picture) is
printed in
the long form of its marker, so that a document always gives a file; the
pieces are reported as errors ({n:print-errors}).

.h3 An exported LaTeX file [print-export-latex]
.ix LaTeX file, from Export
.ix Export a LaTeX File, compiling
{k:F12}, File, Export, Export a LaTeX File ({n:file-export-latex}) saves the file
that the Printer gives to LaTeX, and does not run LaTeX.  The file has a
comment at its top that says how to compile it, and the pictures of the
document are copied into the directory beside it that has the name of the file
and {c:_files} added (the file {c:NAME.tex} has {c:NAME_files}).  It has no
banner, no marks of errors and no Error Log, whatever the document holds.  To
make the pages, run {c:pdflatex} twice on the file; {c:latex} followed by
{c:dvipdfmx} works too.
